<MqttTopicLayout slug="retained-messages">
	<h2>How the retain flag works</h2>
	<p>
		When a message is published with the retain flag set, the broker stores it as the "last known good" value for that
		topic. Any client that subscribes afterward immediately receives that retained message, instead of waiting for the
		next publish. Publishing an empty payload with the retain flag clears it.
	</p>
	<h2>Why it matters</h2>
	<p>
		Retained messages are ideal for state that new subscribers need right away — a device's online status, the latest
		configuration, or the current reading of a sensor — so clients don't start up blind.
	</p>
</MqttTopicLayout>
